    "view": {
      "value": "<div class=\"contentLayout2\">\n<div class=\"columnLayout two-right-sidebar\" data-layout=\"two-right-sidebar\">\n<div class=\"cell normal\" data-type=\"normal\">\n<div class=\"innerCell\">\n<h2 id=\"Radiology-AbouttheFeature\">About the Feature</h2><div>Bahmni supports two ways of managing Radiology workflows:</div><ul><li><p>Via Manual Radiology Upload</p></li><li>Using PACS Integration*<br/><br/></li></ul><div>*Picture Archiving and Communication System (PACS) is a medical imaging technology which provides storage and convenient access to radiology  images from multiple imaging equipments. The images are transmitted digitally from the imaging devices and can be seen using a DICOM image viewer which could be native or web based.</div><div><h2 id=\"Radiology-UsedBy\"><span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\">Used By</span></h2><p><span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\">The orders are usually placed by doctors and sometimes by other staff on behalf of the doctor based on pre-decided protocols. The radiology images are seen by Doctors for diagnostic purposes. </span></p><h2 id=\"Radiology-HowisitUsed?\"><span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\">How is it Used?</span></h2><p>Bahmni supports both PACS integration and manual upload of radiology images. Please refer to the links below for the steps involved in managing Radiology workflows using Bahmni.</p><ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/spaces/BAH/pages/32014462/PACS+Integration+and+Support\" data-linked-resource-id=\"32014462\" data-linked-resource-version=\"8\" data-linked-resource-type=\"page\">Using PACS Integration</a></li><li><p><a href=\"/wiki/spaces/BAH/pages/32014528/Upload+Radiology+Documents\" data-linked-resource-id=\"32014528\" data-linked-resource-version=\"11\" data-linked-resource-type=\"page\">Via Radiology Upload</a></p></li></ul></div></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"cell aside\" data-type=\"aside\">\n<div class=\"innerCell\">\n<div class=\"panel conf-macro output-block\" data-hasbody=\"true\" data-macro-id=\"0add60ca-db50-405a-bfd6-90945fbc2b0b\" data-macro-name=\"panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"panelHeader\" style=\"border-bottom-width: 1px;background-color: #668D3C;color: white;\"><b>Feature Details</b></div><div class=\"panelContent\">\n<p><span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\"><a href=\"/wiki/spaces/BAH/pages/32604202/Radiology+and+PACS\" data-linked-resource-id=\"32604202\" data-linked-resource-version=\"15\" data-linked-resource-type=\"page\">Radiology and PACS - Feature Guide</a></span></p>\n</div></div><div class=\"panel conf-macro output-block\" data-hasbody=\"true\" data-macro-id=\"3fe3feef-06ea-4aac-b9a1-a6bbe83b0bec\" data-macro-name=\"panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"panelHeader\" style=\"border-bottom-width: 1px;background-color: #668D3C;color: white;\"><b>Implemnentation Details</b></div><div class=\"panelContent\">\n<p><span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\"><a href=\"/wiki/spaces/BAH/pages/32014588/Radiology+and+PACS+Integration\" data-linked-resource-id=\"32014588\" data-linked-resource-version=\"48\" data-linked-resource-type=\"page\">Radiology and PACS - Implementer's Guide</a></span></p>\n</div></div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
